consumer-int8-kernels

The integer MMA fragment mapping in csrc/kernels.cu is adapted from
AppMana/forks-flash-mla-int, csrc/debug_imma_sm80.cu (Apache-2.0).
https://github.com/AppMana/forks-flash-mla-int

The Gated DeltaNet decode work partition (four value rows per warp) follows
Don-Chad/ninfer-3090, src/ops/linear_attention/gated_delta_net/recurrent.cuh
at d7277e88cc3a56d2967d5d533f148bed36e97df5 (Apache-2.0).
https://github.com/Don-Chad/ninfer-3090

The chunked GDN prefill adapter instantiates NInfer's prepare_wy_wu,
state_passing and output kernels from the same pinned revision. Their
source and license remain in the third_party/ninfer submodule; the launch
adapter adjusts the scheduling for the actual SM86 device.

The checkpoint channel and group32 encodings match the AppMana vLLM fork's
dsv4_int.py and common/vision_int8.py at
899ced4cf9a4f33f6c0903f3e1858246c63f9fbd (Apache-2.0).
https://github.com/AppMana/forks-vllm-consumer-nvidia-platforms

The SM80 CUTLASS visitor construction in csrc/fused_mm.cu follows vLLM's
csrc/libtorch_stable/quantization/w8a8/cutlass/scaled_mm_c2x.cuh and
cutlass_extensions/epilogue/scaled_mm_epilogues_c2x.hpp at
bfa7e5b7afe40ebe48288801a2baf5c1135cd881 (Apache-2.0).
https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm
The adapter uses ordinary tiled scheduling, BF16 channel scales, and
row-first scaling without an INT32 output workspace.
